---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const areas = await getCollection("locations");
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Houston Area Remodeling Services & Repairs | OilerBilt"
  description="Find OilerBilt remodeling services across Houston, Alief, Mission Bend, Sugar Land, Katy and Missouri City. Check your local service area today."
  breadcrumbLabel="Service Areas"
>
  <div class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a> / Service areas
      </nav>
      <p class="eyebrow">Where we work</p>
      <h1>Houston and southwest Harris County.</h1>
      <p>
        OilerBilt is a service-area contractor. We come to the project; there is
        no public showroom or customer-facing street address.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Choose your remodeling service area</h2>
      <div class="service-grid">
        {areas.map((area) => (
          <a class="service-card" href={`/service-areas/${area.data.slug}/`}>
            <h3>{area.data.title}</h3>
            <p>{area.data.description}</p>
            <span>See local details →</span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
      <article class="article">
        <h2>One metro, several permitting authorities</h2>
        <p>
          A “Houston” mailing address does not always mean a property sits
          inside Houston city limits. Katy, Sugar Land and Missouri City each
          have their own municipal processes, while unincorporated Harris and
          Fort Bend county locations follow different requirements. The scope
          matters too: paint and cabinet replacement are not treated the same
          way as moving plumbing, electrical systems or structural walls.
        </p>
        <p>
          We confirm the project address and requested changes before answering
          permit questions. That short check is more useful than a generic
          promise that every remodel needs a permit or none do.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
